#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""zstates: does AllowZstates start runtime S0i2 in the bit-16 idle state? (#249, kernel 9.111 or later)

On 9.110 idlemask bit 16 read idle at runtime once the PSP was runtime-suspended and the
keyboard/Bluetooth xHCI (67:00.0) was asleep, with the screen really off and display idle
allowed (the g-plus and g-hold kits); every bit of the runtime gate mask 0x07C39109 read idle
except bit 8. The SMU's timein_s0i2 still stayed 0 and socket power didn't drop. The SMU image
suggests its runtime deep-idle gate also needs a Z-state enable fed by AllowZstates
(PPSMC_MSG_AllowZstates 0x25), which Linux never sends. 9.111 added the debugfs switch
dri/<amdgpu minor>/amdgpu_smu_allow_zstates (patch 9910; 0, 8 or 9), and lets the built-in
keyboard (0b05:19b6) autosuspend: hid-asus declares only its Caps Lock LED (9909) and
omarchy-asus-g16's udev rule (1.0.0-104 and later) puts it on power/control=auto. Every
linux-omarchy since carries 9901-9910 (7.2.15-1.101 does), so the installed kernel runs it:
no test kernel, no reboot.

One question: in the idle state where bit 16 clears, does sending AllowZstates (9, then 8)
make the SMU enter runtime S0i2 (timein_s0i2 rising, battery power dropping)?

  K   the keyboard, screen on. K0 as installed (nothing changed): does 3-4 autosuspend by
      itself (9909 + the udev rule)? K1 Bluetooth soft-blocked: does 67:00.0 sleep too? Only if
      not: K2 asusd, g16-winlockd and the user's g16-winlock stopped, the keyboard's LEDs and
      backlight off (the g-hold B state); only if still not: K3 the keyboard deauthorized.
      Up to 10 s each, runtime_status at 10 Hz.
  key the keyboard asleep, the key check: the run log says "press Shift once"; the kit reads
      the keyboard's event nodes (read only, no grab) and its runtime_status at 20 Hz for up
      to 45 s: did the press wake it, and was the press itself delivered (a Shift press
      before its release) or lost? No press in the window: not checked, the run goes on.
  G   amdgpu.dcn35_s0i2=1 and amdgpu.dm_idle_all_off=1 (set with the screen on), the screen
      off (DPMS; verified by Hyprland's dpmsStatus AND the eDP connector's kernel DPMS
      state), the PSP runtime-suspended (ccp.psp_rpm_delay_ms=2000 + power/control=auto,
      9906); then up to 15 s for bit 16 to read idle.
  Z   30 s each: base (nothing sent), AllowZstates(9), AllowZstates(8), AllowZstates(0) (the
      restore). The idlemask, the screen, 3-4, 67:00.0, the PSP and battery watts at 1 Hz; at each phase's
      start and end only: SMU metrics (9907 smu_metrics_runtime: timein_s0i2 and the per-IP
      "time condition not met" counters), RAPL package energy, gpu_metrics socket power,
      every CPU's cpuidle usage and time (wakeups/s) and /proc/interrupts;
      display idle (amdgpu_dm_ips_status "Idle optimization"). A phase is INVALID unless the
      screen reads off by both checks at its start and end and in 90% of the 1 Hz reads,
      the PSP stays suspended, and 67:00.0 is asleep in 90% of reads; an INVALID phase is
      run once more.
Stops early: no base in the idle state (bit 16 idle in under 80% of reads): no message is
sent. AllowZstates(9) clearly starts S0i2 (timein_s0i2 grows by 10% of the phase or more
AND battery power drops 0.2 W or more): 8 is skipped. Neither 9 nor 8 changes anything: 0
is sent without a measured phase.

  zstates               run it: on battery, one root prompt, about 4 minutes; hands off
                        except one Shift press when the run log asks (about 30 s in)
  zstates --check       read-only preflight as you (no root, nothing changed)
  zstates --dry-run     the whole run against a fake sysfs tree in a temporary directory,
                        with a kernel emulator; no root, nothing on this machine changed
                        (--sim-kbd k0|k1|k2|k3: the level at which the keyboard sleeps;
                         --sim-udev yes|no: whether the udev rule set power/control=auto;
                         --sim-z z9|z8|counter|drop|none: what the messages do;
                         --sim-key kept|lost|none: the Shift press;
                         --sim-state ok|nobit16|screen: the idle state)

Never: the eDP connector's `status` (force-off froze Hyprland), recursive sysfs globs, NVRAM
or BIOS writes, the RTX or anything under it (64:00.x), the global ASPM policy, unbinding a
driver, loading modules, audio (nothing makes a sound), Wi-Fi (it stays on).

Everything goes back on exit from an undo journal under /run (the keyboard first, then newest
first): AllowZstates(0) if the last value sent wasn't 0, the LEDs' triggers and brightness,
asusd, g16-winlockd and g16-winlock, power/control values, Bluetooth, the parameters, the
PSP's runtime PM, DPMS on. A root watchdog unit does the same if the kit dies or passes its
deadline. The SMU's Z-state setting isn't readable back; a reboot resets it.

Root: pkexec through the desktop's polkit agent (G16_POLKIT_REASON=<wrapper> runs
`<wrapper> run REASON -- pkexec ...`; G16_ROOT=sudo uses sudo).
Exit status: 0 the run finished (whatever the verdict), 1 a problem, 2 bad usage.
"""
